        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "86a05e8e-240e-5653-acf1-1acf707b5b4c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Harold Godwinson, Harald Hardrada, William the Conqueror, Tostig Godwinson, Eystein Orre\n- Events: Battle of Stamford Bridge, Battle of Hastings\n- Places: Stamford Bridge, East Riding of Yorkshire, England, Norway\n\nFacts:\n- On 25 September 1066, the Battle of Stamford Bridge took place at the village of Stamford Bridge in the East Riding of Yorkshire, England.\n- The Battle of Stamford Bridge was fought between an English army under King Harold Godwinson and an invading Norwegian force led by King Harald Hardrada and Tostig Godwinson.\n- On 25 September 1066, Harold Godwinson defeated and killed Harald Hardrada at the Battle of Stamford Bridge.\n- Eystein Orre was a Norwegian noble who died on 25 September 1066 after being killed at the Battle of Stamford Bridge.\n- In October 1066, William the Conqueror defeated and killed Harold Godwinson at the Battle of Hastings.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "249b8ed0-ef7d-58ce-bbdb-6fe69a04968c",
        "text": "Page: Ancestry of the Godwins. Sentence: In September 1066 Harold defeated and killed King Harald Hardrada of Norway at the Battle of Stamford Bridge, and Harold was himself defeated and killed the following month by William the Conqueror at the Battle of Hastings.\nPage: Battle of Stamford Bridge. Sentence: The Battle of Stamford Bridge took place at the village of Stamford Bridge, East Riding of Yorkshire, in England on 25 September 1066, between an English army under King Harold Godwinson and an invading Norwegian force led by King Harald Hardrada and the English king's brother Tostig Godwinson.\nPage: Eystein Orre. Sentence: Eystein Orre (Old Norse: \"Eystein Orri\"; died 25 September 1066) was a Norwegian noble who was killed at the Battle of Stamford Bridge in 1066.",
